# --- s040 Book I d.11 q.1 = Ord. I d.11 q.1
n("n675","s040-01","Circa distinctionem vndecimam","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 11 q. 1, *utrum Spiritus Sanctus procedat a Patre et Filio* (Vat. V). Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 11.","to-verify")
n("n676","s040-01","Damascenus. c. 7.","la","source","John Damascene, *De fide orthodoxa* I c. 8 (Burgundio's Latin; ‘c. 7’ in the medieval capitulation): the Spirit *ex Patre procedens et in Filio quiescens*, as cited in Scotus's opening argument. The chapter number and the exact Latin wording are to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n677","s040-01","ex patre filioque procedit","la","source","The Niceno-Constantinopolitan Creed in its Latin liturgical form, with the *Filioque*.","certain")
n("n678","s040-01","Atanasius in symbolo","la","source","*Symbolum Quicumque* (‘Athanasian’ Creed): *Spiritus Sanctus a Patre et Filio, non factus nec creatus nec genitus, sed procedens*.","certain")
n("n679","s040-01","Henricus quodlibeto. 6° q. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* VI q. 1. The reference is as printed; Henry's discussion of the order of productions is also in *Summa* a. 54 and a. 60.","to-verify")
n("n680","s040-03","dictum Andree","la","source","*Passio sancti Andreae* (the ‘Letter of the presbyters and deacons of Achaia’), in Andrew's confession: *Spiritum Sanctum ex Patre procedentem et in Filio permanentem*. Cited in the *Filioque* controversy (e.g. Anselm, Aquinas, *Contra errores Graecorum*).","to-verify")
n("n681","s040-03","Si ascendero in celum mittam vobis paraclitum","la","source","A paraphrase, not a verbatim Vulgate text: cf. John 16:7 *si autem abiero, mittam eum ad vos*; John 15:26 *cum autem venerit Paraclitus quem ego mittam vobis a Patre*.","certain")
n("n682","s040-03","Ille me clarificabit qui de meo accipiet","la","source","John 16:14 (Vulg.): *ille me clarificabit quia de meo accipiet*. A has *qui* for *quia*.","certain")
n("n683","s040-03","insufflauit","la","source","John 20:22: *insufflavit et dicit eis: Accipite Spiritum Sanctum*.","certain")
n("n684","s040-03","Athanasius grecus","la","historical","The Greek Fathers adduced for the *Filioque* (Athanasius, Dionysius, Chrysostom) form a standard Latin dossier (cf. Aquinas, *Contra errores Graecorum*; Council of Florence debates). Specific passages are not given.","to-verify")
n("n685","s040-03","de summa trini. extra. c. 1.","la","source","*Liber Extra* X 1.1.1 *Firmiter* (Lateran IV, 1215): *Spiritus Sanctus ab utroque*.","certain")
n("n686","s040-04","quatuor conclusiones","la","source","On *a Patre per Filium*: Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 12 q. 2 (and d. 11 q. 1). The rejection of the Son as *principium quo*, as instrument, and as secondary cause is the standard scholastic analysis (cf. Aquinas, *ST* I q. 36 a. 3).","to-verify")
n("n687","s040-05","Aug. 9. de trini.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* IX (mind, knowledge, love) and XV 21.41 (memory, understanding, will). The terminology *memoria fecunda / voluntas fecunda* is Scotist (*Ord.* I d. 2 p. 2 qq. 1–4; d. 10).","to-verify")
n("n688","s040-06","Aureolus","la","historical","Peter Auriol (d. 1322), *Scriptum super I Sent.* d. 11 (or d. 26–28 on the constitution of the persons). Gorris names Auriol here; the exact locus is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n689","s040-06","Sed doctoris est opinio","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 11 q. 2 / d. 28 q. 3: active spiration is not constitutive, since the persons are understood as constituted prior to the fruitful volition.","to-verify")
n("n690","s040-04","principle by which","en","translation","*principium quo* (the formal principle) vs *principium quod* (the supposit that acts).")
n("n691","s040-03","abides in the Son","en","translation","*permanere*; Damascene's *quiescere* (‘rest’) in 01.")

